From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shi Jiayang <shi05275@163.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mediatek: disable TX offload for YT922x tags

The MTK hardware parser cannot handle the eight-byte YT922x CPU tag when
calculating transport checksums or performing TCP segmentation. Packets
with partial checksums can therefore be transmitted with invalid checksums.

Extend the existing per-skb DSA feature check so the networking core
performs software segmentation and checksum completion for YT922x
conduits. Retain hardware offload for all other conduit protocols.

Signed-off-by: Shi Jiayang <shi05275@163.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -5139,7 +5139,8 @@ static netdev_features_t mtk_features_ch
 		 * software before appending the tag, so ip_summed is no longer
 		 * CHECKSUM_PARTIAL by the time this driver sees it.
 		 */
-		if (tag_ops->proto == DSA_TAG_PROTO_RTL8_4)
+		if (tag_ops->proto == DSA_TAG_PROTO_RTL8_4 ||
+		    tag_ops->proto == DSA_TAG_PROTO_YT922X)
 			features &= ~(NETIF_F_CSUM_MASK | NETIF_F_GSO_MASK);
 	}
 
